Z||000000||rogergarrison||11-08-2001||04:43 PM||||Been so long on my 86 i forgot. Is 88 front bearings any diff from 86 to replace. I know theres some suspension changes. Dont want to get involved in a big deal. I need to put in inner and outer.||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||11-08-2001||06:06 PM||||88 is a hub/bearing assembly similar to the rears. You have to replace the whole thing. Last I heard there weren't any new ones available. I got mine from Autozone last spring, but checked recently and they are out of stock. I've heard Timken quit making them... I've also heard they may just make them on infrequent lot runs. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||11-08-2001||09:40 PM||||Roger,<P>They attach the same way the rear hub/bearing assemblies do.<BR>Somebody on here mentioned that they had a line on them. Maybe post in the mall, if you haven't already.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||11-08-2001||10:11 PM||||If you cannot find any new ones, give Kick Hill, Bob Steiger, or whoever your favorite used Fiero parts vendor is and get some good used ones.  I know they aren't new, but as long as they don't have a ton of milage on them they should last a while!  I also think I remember someone mentioning their shop had success in rebuilding them.  I dunno what the cost would be but the thread is somewhere on the forum!||||reg||1
